  "question": {
    "text": "An open glass tube is immersed in mercury in such a way that a length of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>8</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math> extends above the mercury level. The open end of the tube is then closed and sealed and the tube is raised vertically up by additional <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>46</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math>. What will be length of the air column above mercury in the tube now ?<br />(Atmospheric pressure = <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>76</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math> of Hg)"
